{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said to Moses: Do not fear him.</b> Rashi explained: he needed to say 'do not fear him' regarding Og, which he did not need to say regarding Sihon, because he feared lest Og's merit stand for him, since he told Abraham our father that Lot was captured. And if you ask: was not his intention for evil, so that Abraham would be killed and he could take Sarah? — one may answer: since deliverance came through him, he had reason to fear, just as we find in the chapter חלק regarding the merit of the forty-two offerings that Balak offered — he merited and Ruth came forth from him, even though he intended only for evil, to curse Israel. However, it is a difficulty according to the one who says that Og was called 'the fugitive' (פליט) because he escaped from the Flood — for in tractate נדה it is concluded that Og and Sihon were brothers, and if so, where do we find that Sihon escaped from the Flood? Granted, regarding Og we find an allusion and hint, as I explained in the portion of נח in the name of R. Judah the Pious: ״וישאר אך נח״ — which adds up in gematria to עוג. But for Sihon we find no hint. My master Rabbi Yechiel bar Joseph said that Og was born before the Flood, and his mother was pregnant with Sihon in the year of the Flood; she went and married one of the sons of Noah, and she was already pregnant from those sons of the Elohim who took from the daughters of men, and Sihon was born in the ark."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {0 "The bracketed words [היכן מצינו] appear to be a editorial restoration; translated as part of the sentence. The phrase 'ואו׳ הרב רב יחיאל' reads 'and my master Rabbi Yechiel said' — 'רב' taken as an honorific title."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:58.815243161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}